{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1078007-rotes-of-life-1-3","id":1078007,"title":"Rotes of Life 1-3","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-13T16:15:21-07:00","id":1078007,"title":"Rotes of Life 1-3","content":"Use your imagination and tell me your most creative ideas for Life sphere.!<br /> <br /> On serious note, I need few ideas","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13055-goran","name":"Goran.","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T20:20:55-07:00","id":1078141,"title":"","content":"Life 2: Alter the cells inside a large fruit to have box jellyfish nematocysts for the duration of 1 day. Carefully make juice. Spray enemies with juice or get them to drink it somehow. The nematocysts vanish after a day.<br /> Life 2: Find a large simple life form such as a very large squid. Replace the squid ink gland with Golden Orb Weaver Silk Glands. Yank the squid out of water and pester it for as long as you can. It will spray silk that can be made into material that is stronger than kevlar.<br /> Life 2: Get an Ascomycete fungus (Truffle). Give it the ability to thrive in any soil, grow quickly like bamboo, and sprout multiple truffles. Sell the resulting truffles for profit.<br /> Life 2: Enchant mollusk to grow sharp flat shells in the shape of a dagger and out of the same material as limpet teeth to make for an extremely sharp, sturdy, and non-metal knife.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T20:25:48-07:00","id":1078147,"title":"","content":"My question would be for what focus/paradigm?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T09:10:49-07:00","id":1078388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1078007-rotes-of-life-1-3?p=1078147#post1078147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My question would be for what focus/paradigm?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just write your ideas. Everything you have.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13055-goran","name":"Goran.","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T17:19:14-07:00","id":1079126,"title":"","content":"Life 1 &quot;life vision&quot;. It's the poorman's heat vision. Depending on your paradigm, you'll either &quot;feel&quot; the vibrations of nature, or literally see all life patterns immediately in front of you. If you're in a dark forest, you'll be able to see or sense your way around the trees and any wildelife that wonders by.<br /> <br /> Life 1 &quot;How hurt is it?&quot; This allows you to know exactly how many Health Levels something has and is at. Mix with Entropy 1 to see how close to death they are, adding Time 1 to sense an accurate &quot;death clock&quot;.<br /> <br /> Life 3 &quot;Modesty Scales&quot;. This is what happens when a Verbena goes skyclad into the umbra for the first time, but isn't actually all that comfortable with being nude.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T18:16:44-07:00","id":1079142,"title":"","content":"Life 3 - Shapechanging and appearance modification. Alter eye, skin, and hair color. Reshape the face into someone else's, or an original face. Make oneself taller, shorter, thinner, fatter, or alter the overall body shape completely. Modify the shape of the vocal chords, so as to alter the voice. Even without getting animal or plant features involved, this is a powerful application of Life.<br /> <br /> Life 3 - Grow the hair out, and command it to move. Suddenly, you've got deadly hair, capable of grappling, striking, or strangling. Might only work for mystic Paradigms, as technomancers will likely see hair as dead, inert Matter, even if it's still attached to the head.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T19:46:17-07:00","id":1079181,"title":"","content":"Life 2: Get an Asian Giant Hornet. Give it Mantis Shrimp or Pistol Shrimp Claws. Give it a boost of whatever hormone makes such creatures highly aggressive. Give it more potent venom or bombardier beetle spray if you like. Cool it down, put it in a paper bag, and leave it in the office of a foe.<br /> <br /> Life 3: Give yourself the equivalent of Mantis Shrimp or Pistol Shrimp Claws. Learn Kung Fu.<br /> <br /> Life 2: Have all the indoor plants in a house produce hydrogen cyanide like an irritated millipede. If the inhabitants aren't killed by the poison gas, set the place on fire. Hydrogen cyanide is explosive.<br /> <br /> Life 3: Use your powers of healing to hide a tiny non-metal metaphysical link for correspondence effects underneath someone's skin... preferably while they are unconscious and unaware.<br /> <br /> Life 2: Cause certain crabs to molt so that you can have soft-shelled crab any day of the year.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T20:39:49-07:00","id":1079206,"title":"","content":"Personally, I see Life 2 as being about manipulating a body's autonomous functions, of which healing and harm are only two. While it can't alter anything, it can make the bodies do particular things on command. At Life 3, you can start doing this to other people.<br /> <br /> <br /> Life 2 - Smoke cigarettes with impunity, by automatically flushing toxins from the body, and repairing the small damages that could lead to medical problems down the road. Better yet, weave this enchantment into a pipe as an Artifact or Talisman, so you don't need to fiddle with separate Instruments every time you want a smoke. Since it's an Artifact or Wonder, it only takes a single success to work.<br /> <br /> Life 2 - Cause your body to produce sweat and skin oil in excess, increasing difficulties for others to grapple you. At Life 3, you can force an enemy to sweat until they suffer dehydration.<br /> <br /> Life 3 - Brown Note. 'Nuff said. Could work going back up, too.<br /> <br /> Life 3 - Give a regular, edible mushroom the poisonous properties of the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amanita_phalloides\" target=\"_blank\">Death Cap</a> or <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Destroying_angel\" target=\"_blank\">Destroying Angel</a>. These mushrooms are diabolical, especially since they are not only (very) toxic, but the life-threatening symptoms tend to crop up long after the damage becomes irreparable. Within the first day to two of ingestion, the person is hit by intestinal trouble (diarrhea and vomiting), but which might not be serious enough to warrant an emergency room. Then those symptoms improve, and the next week the victim feels normal. By this point, the person is a dead man walking, as they succumb to intestinal and kidney failure, as well as perhaps cardiac arrest. Treatment is possible if the poisoning is caught quick enough, but results aren't guaranteed. In extreme cases, liver transplants are necessary, which is also not guaranteed to help. There is no antidote, only general treatments.<br /> <br /> Seriously, these mushrooms are horrifying. I wouldn't wish such a fate on my worst enemy. Use with discretion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T23:15:29-07:00","id":1079255,"title":"","content":"Life 1 - By comparing a subject's form with their underlying Pattern, you should be able to see if a creature has shapeshifted. With sufficient successes, they might even be able to determine their true form.<br /> <br /> Life 2 - Hungry? Find a tree, and cause it to bear fruit. Potentially, even if the tree normally produces no fruit. Variants might include promoting the growth of mycelia in the soil, sprouting edible mushrooms from the ground. (As pointed out in my previous post, it's prudent to only promote the growth of edible fungi. A simple Life 1 scan will be sufficient to find the right varieties).<br /> <br /> (If you're amenable to conjunctional Effects, may I recommend one I invented a while back. Life 2 + Forces 3 to convert sunlight directly into nourishment. Like a tree, you feed upon the rays of the sun, skipping that tedious &quot;food&quot; nonsense).<br /> <br /> Life 2 - Kill the bacteria and viruses inside food and drink.<br /> <br /> Life 3 - By controlling another's body functions, you can force their limbs into muscle spasms, contracting or loosening muscles as needed. Affect a leg, and it can force them to trip or fall over. Weaken the muscles in the hand, and it can be forced to drop a weapon. With sufficient successes, you can even command the person with a crude form of meat puppetry. Instead of directing them through mind control, it's through body control. True, intricate control may require Life 4, at Storyteller's choice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T02:15:04-07:00","id":1079299,"title":"","content":"Life 3: Give yourself the ability to regenerate a whole body from a single arm, like a starfish. Make sure this effect is long lasting. Cut your arm off. Wait for your arm to regenerate and a body to regenerate from your arm. Speed the process using healing life magick. Now you have a complete physical copy of yourself that's likely a vegetable or with the mind of an infant.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T03:07:49-07:00","id":1079310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1078007-rotes-of-life-1-3?p=1079299#post1079299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Life 3: Give yourself the ability to regenerate a whole body from a single arm, like a starfish. Make sure this effect is long lasting. Cut your arm off. Wait for your arm to regenerate and a body to regenerate from your arm. Speed the process using healing life magick. Now you have a complete physical copy of yourself that's likely a vegetable or with the mind of an infant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically the severed arm falls under matter as it is not alive just meat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T05:36:55-07:00","id":1079336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1078007-rotes-of-life-1-3?p=1079310#post1079310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technically the severed arm falls under matter as it is not alive just meat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not quite. As long as the organ or meat is in a state where it could still be preserved and transplanted, it continues to fall under Life. Only when it's dead-dead does it become matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T05:50:02-07:00","id":1079339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1078007-rotes-of-life-1-3?p=1079336#post1079336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not quite. As long as the organ or meat is in a state where it could still be preserved and transplanted, it continues to fall under Life. Only when it's dead-dead does it become matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>In that case if trying to regenerate another body separate from the original pattern is life 4?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T13:59:23-07:00","id":1079503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1078007-rotes-of-life-1-3?p=1079299#post1079299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Life 3: Give yourself the ability to regenerate a whole body from a single arm, like a starfish. Make sure this effect is long lasting. Cut your arm off. Wait for your arm to regenerate and a body to regenerate from your arm. Speed the process using healing life magick. Now you have a complete physical copy of yourself that's likely a vegetable or with the mind of an infant.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really see this as trying to rationalize a way around the Life 5 requirement to create life. Now granted it is only creating copies of you but Life 4 would atleast be required to create complex organs and maintian actual life. Even then I'm not sure I'd allow it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T07:15:37-07:00","id":1079778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1078007-rotes-of-life-1-3?p=1079255#post1079255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Life 3 - By controlling another's body functions, you can force their limbs into muscle spasms, contracting or loosening muscles as needed. Affect a leg, and it can force them to trip or fall over. Weaken the muscles in the hand, and it can be forced to drop a weapon. With sufficient successes, you can even command the person with a crude form of meat puppetry. Instead of directing them through mind control, it's through body control. True, intricate control may require Life 4, at Storyteller's choice.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a pretty interesting effect. I always thought about controlling someone else's bosy to make them sleep or give them convulsions, but controlling their muscles is even better. Would it be possible to make them attack someone? Or flee? Or even say something that they don't want to someone. Afterall, everything we do is result of our body motions or chemistry. One can control the lungs, vocal chords tongue and lips to make someone talk exactly what he wants...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T09:29:01-07:00","id":1079831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tuch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1078007-rotes-of-life-1-3?p=1079503#post1079503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really see this as trying to rationalize a way around the Life 5 requirement to create life. Now granted it is only creating copies of you but Life 4 would atleast be required to create complex organs and maintian actual life. Even then I'm not sure I'd allow it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I'm not going to debate about the actual legality of this in a particular game. I'm just putting this out there as something that could supposedly be done by a flat reading of the rules without bothering with any context whatsoever. Just to be specific, Life magick was only used to grant a creature quality and yes it is blatant loophole exploitation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":". 04-17-2017, 12:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T11:00:36-07:00","id":1079875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1078007-rotes-of-life-1-3?p=1079778#post1079778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a pretty interesting effect. I always thought about controlling someone else's bosy to make them sleep or give them convulsions, but controlling their muscles is even better. Would it be possible to make them attack someone? Or flee? Or even say something that they don't want to someone. Afterall, everything we do is result of our body motions or chemistry. One can control the lungs, vocal chords tongue and lips to make someone talk exactly what he wants...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, although it probably wouldn't easy. Lots of successes required, and a fair Storyteller would allow the (conscious) victim to make resistance rolls with either Willpower or Stamina. If the mage can overcome this, though, then they would, indeed, have a living meat puppet.<br /> <br /> Again, however, a Storyteller would be well within their rights to make full puppetry the province of Life 4. With Life 3 only allowing for momentary, directed muscles spasms (nothing for full combat actions like Attacking or Movement).<br /> <br /> On the plus side, controlling a person's diaphragm in order to inhibit breathing falls squarely under Life 3, since you're trying to damage them (albeit with suffocation).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T11:12:19-07:00","id":1079884,"title":"","content":"Life 3: Thicken your skin and then give yourself the ability to shed your skin like a snake. Make the most awful costumes ever.<br /> Life 3: Give yourself radiation resistance like a tardigrade. Meet your foes while carrying highly radioactive material. Decontaminate before the duration of your magick ends.<br /> Life 3: Give yourself electricity producing organs and electricity storing electrocytes. Attach these to some sort of electric device you could use to charge your electronics if you continuously discharge the right amount of electric current. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T11:14:46-07:00","id":1079886,"title":"","content":"Say, could you use life 3 to give someone hiccups?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T12:05:12-07:00","id":1079918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1078007-rotes-of-life-1-3?p=1079875#post1079875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, although it probably wouldn't easy. Lots of successes required, and a fair Storyteller would allow the (conscious) victim to make resistance rolls with either Willpower or Stamina. If the mage can overcome this, though, then they would, indeed, have a living meat puppet.<br /> <br /> Again, however, a Storyteller would be well within their rights to make full puppetry the province of Life 4. With Life 3 only allowing for momentary, directed muscles spasms (nothing for full combat actions like Attacking or Movement).<br /> <br /> On the plus side, controlling a person's diaphragm in order to inhibit breathing falls squarely under Life 3, since you're trying to damage them (albeit with suffocation).</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe a resisted roll should be made, but wouldn't it be necessary in Mind effect too?<br /> Life 4 allows other people complete transfiguration, which is way more complex than muscle control. You're not even transforming anything, I'd say it's Life 3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T13:15:23-07:00","id":1079950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe a resisted roll should be made, but wouldn't it be necessary in Mind effect too?<br /> Life 4 allows other people complete transfiguration, which is way more complex than muscle control. You're not even transforming anything, I'd say it's Life 3.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that this effect exists in the Revised Corebook as a Life rote (or as part of the Life Sphere), and it was Life 4. Don't remember why.<br /> <br /> You don't need Mind because you're controling the person physically, without touching her perception, thought or cognition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T14:34:04-07:00","id":1080003,"title":"","content":"Life 3 - Give yourself literal eyes in the back of your head, so you can never be sneaked up on. With the proper headware - like a helmet with holes in the back that are big enough for you to see through but small enough that others can't - it might even be coincidental.<br /> <br /> Life 3 - Toss a gun into a patch of tall grass. Proceed to animate that grass, so it can manipulate the gun. You now have a secondary, hidden &quot;sniper&quot;, from which you can take potshots at people. Might induce an increase to difficulty on the Dex + Firearms roll (assuming you aren't using something like Manipulation instead), unless the character either has an active Correspondence 1 effect, or has a Firearms specialty in indirect firing or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T19:07:05-07:00","id":1080134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1078007-rotes-of-life-1-3?p=1079950#post1079950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that this effect exists in the Revised Corebook as a Life rote (or as part of the Life Sphere), and it was Life 4. Don't remember why.<br /> <br /> You don't need Mind because you're controling the person physically, without touching her perception, thought or cognition.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What I meant was: wouldn`t the effect need a resisted roll if it was a Mind effect instead of a Life one? Using Mind to control somebody doesn`t need resisted rolls too?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T06:32:25-07:00","id":1080290,"title":"","content":"Here's a few my group is fond of.<br /> <br /> Life 3. Deaden Pain Receptors: removes combat wound modifers.<br /> <br /> Life 2: Go Without: able to go without food, water and sleep for 24 hours (we require 1 point of quintessence as well)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T08:17:55-07:00","id":1080328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I meant was: wouldn`t the effect need a resisted roll if it was a Mind effect instead of a Life one? Using Mind to control somebody doesn`t need resisted rolls too?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, indeed, you can roll Willpower as a &quot;dodge&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T18:10:54-07:00","id":1080670,"title":"","content":"Life 2 - Cause a tree to grow the tiny, poisonous hairs of the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dendrocnide_moroides\" target=\"_blank\">Australian Stinging Tree</a>, and trick an enemy into touching it. You know, if you're a <b>sadistic monster.</b><br /> <br /> Life 1 - Studying the rapidly decaying flesh - and the tiny decomposers that inhabit it - determine when a corpse died, and how. (Certain sources from Mage maintain that a corpse can still be manipulated with Life, while skeletons require Matter; see the Rotes for animating corpses).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T02:30:07-07:00","id":1080792,"title":"","content":"What would a fruit be classified as? A simple life form or the rough equivalent of a simple life-form corpse?<br /> I'm trying to think what you'd need to have a fruit grow legs and walk<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T07:54:37-07:00","id":1080891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1078007-rotes-of-life-1-3?p=1080792#post1080792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would a fruit be classified as? A simple life form or the rough equivalent of a simple life-form corpse?<br /> I'm trying to think what you'd need to have a fruit grow legs and walk<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I remember an example of turning an apple into a solid golden apple as a Life 2 / Matter 2 effect. It was in a core book, probably 2nd or revised. So Life 2 sounds good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T11:44:25-07:00","id":1081011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1078007-rotes-of-life-1-3?p=1080891#post1080891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I remember an example of turning an apple into a solid golden apple as a Life 2 / Matter 2 effect. It was in a core book, probably 2nd or revised. So Life 2 sounds good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool. Then you could get a fruits to dip themselves in sweetened cream and hop into people's dessert bowls.<br /> while you use Life or Matter 2 &amp; Prime 2 to have a roast cow walk up to each banquet guest as a server follows it around and slices pieces from it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T23:46:41-07:00","id":1081333,"title":"","content":"Life 2 - Promote the growth of bacteria on someone's food as they eat it, inducing food poisoning. Good for covertly getting some away from a dinner table and towards the nearest restroom (or ambulance, as the case may be).<br /> <br /> Life 2 - Speed up the rate of fermentation, so it produces alcohol faster. Cut the brewing time drastically. Just remember to keep everything sealed and clean, or you might end up spoiling the whole stock.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T23:47:29-07:00","id":1081334,"title":"","content":"Yeah, a zombie cow asks you what part of it you prefer.<br /> Matter 3, Prime 2, Forces 2<br /> Add Mind 5 or Spirit 3 if you don't want to bother with the dialogue yourself.<br /> <br /> I think for the different types of steaks (medium, well done and rare) Matter 3 would be needed. Forces for the sound manipulation to give the cow a proper voice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":12022,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","user":"Nonsense","date":". 04-20-2017, 02:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T23:59:30-07:00","id":1081338,"title":"","content":"Can you think about more combat use of Life 2-3?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13055-goran","name":"Goran.","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T00:07:22-07:00","id":1081342,"title":"","content":"Life 3) Popcorn hornets, turn an ear of corn into a swarm of stinging hornets. Big success get you the thumb sized ones from Japan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T07:57:57-07:00","id":1081439,"title":"","content":"Life 3, to change size of animal. Make your attack dog the size of a horse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T12:12:09-07:00","id":1081530,"title":"","content":"In terms of combat, using Life 2 to make a swarm of super poisonous/venomous, flying, amphibious, fast healing, regenerating, aggressive bugs with bullet shrimp claws, tardigrade level resilience, and camouflage should be fun.<br /> <br /> Then you could emit phermones so that you can direct the creatures as their queen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T12:25:19-07:00","id":1081537,"title":"","content":"Hmmm, I suspect that Spacecat is having a little too much fun with this one...<br /> <br /> How to stop your players getting away with wacky shit 101:<br /> <br /> - Any attempt to control a living being like a puppet should also require Mind 4<br /> - Any attempt to increase size should require Prime 2 (and possibly some quintessence) to create the additional flesh out of thin air<br /> - Multiple simultaneous effects should get a difficulty penalty - at least +1 for each two effects/spheres<br /> - Any 'clever' ideas should require a degree of skill (equal to sphere rating) in a suitable subject for the paradigm<br /> e.g.<br /> - - Anything to do with poisons should require the Poison skill (or Chemistry at a penalty)<br /> - - Anything to do with modifying plants should require Science (Botany)<br /> - - Anything to do with modifying animals should require Science (Zoology or Vetinarian)<br /> - - Any healing should require some medical skill - or something appropriate to the healing paradigm such as Esoterica (Reiki Healing)<br /> <br /> Creating an effect is not just about having the right spheres, the mage also needs the knowledge to encompass the effect they are creating!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11490,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","user":"Dogstar","date":". 04-20-2017, 03:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T13:00:11-07:00","id":1081548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1078007-rotes-of-life-1-3?p=1081537#post1081537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm, I suspect that Spacecat is having a little too much fun with this one...<br /> <br /> How to stop your players getting away with wacky shit 101:<br /> <br /> - Any attempt to control a living being like a puppet should also require Mind 4<br /> - Any attempt to increase size should require Prime 2 (and possibly some quintessence) to create the additional flesh out of thin air<br /> - Multiple simultaneous effects should get a difficulty penalty - at least +1 for each two effects/spheres<br /> - Any 'clever' ideas should require a degree of skill (equal to sphere rating) in a suitable subject for the paradigm<br /> e.g.<br /> - - Anything to do with poisons should require the Poison skill (or Chemistry at a penalty)<br /> - - Anything to do with modifying plants should require Science (Botany)<br /> - - Anything to do with modifying animals should require Science (Zoology or Vetinarian)<br /> - - Any healing should require some medical skill - or something appropriate to the healing paradigm such as Esoterica (Reiki Healing)<br /> <br /> Creating an effect is not just about having the right spheres, the mage also needs the knowledge to encompass the effect they are creating!</div> </div> </div> </div>Lets still have fun with it:<br /> <br /> -No need to micromanage. Just make sure they don't eat me and kinda use me as home base. Phermones should do the trick<br /> -No change in size. I don't want them to be big targets<br /> -So let's see, a giant wasp already flies and is aggressive (or phermones could do that later), let's just make it super poisonous, fast healing, regenerating, with bullet shrimp claws, with tardigrade level resilience, and camouflage for a +3 and spend 3 quintessence to lower the difficulty per roll (You get what you pay for). Then do a long long ritual. Make sure you pump your stamina first. Or if that's still unmanageable, just leave the super poisonous and add one more quality, like camouflage or regeneration... or the claws. Maybe you don't actually get a swarm but just a bunch of these should do the trick.<br /> -Make sure you are a biologist or a nature mage<br /> <br /> <br /> Also: You can direct these stupid things with Mind 3 by using the equivalent of mental illusions on them. It's not puppet control, but it should suffice for general combat directions of designating enemies, things to avoid, and waypoints.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":". 04-20-2017, 04:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T13:50:20-07:00","id":1081567,"title":"","content":"On that note<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1078007-rotes-of-life-1-3?p=1081537#post1081537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How to stop your players getting away with wacky shit 101:</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't want your mage players to do weird stuff?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1078007-rotes-of-life-1-3?p=1081537#post1081537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Any attempt to increase size should require Prime 2 (and possibly some quintessence) to create the additional flesh out of thin air</div> </div> </div> </div>Couldn't you use something other than prime if you want to make the mass out of something else and not create it from nothing? Say making it out of matter or forces?<br /> It is Life 5/ Forces 3 to change people into electricity after all (page 516 M20) so changing electricity into bug mass should just be Forces 3 Life 2<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1078007-rotes-of-life-1-3?p=1081537#post1081537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Any 'clever' ideas should require a degree of skill (equal to sphere rating) in a suitable subject for the paradigm</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, but....<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1078007-rotes-of-life-1-3?p=1081537#post1081537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- - Anything to do with poisons should require the Poison skill (or Chemistry at a penalty)</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a poison skill? What if your paradigm doesn't deal with chemistry? What if you just know all the most poisonous creatures in your land and use sympathetic magic?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1078007-rotes-of-life-1-3?p=1081537#post1081537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- - Anything to do with modifying plants should require Science (Botany)</div> </div> </div> </div>So your nature shaman who is one with the forest should know science?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1078007-rotes-of-life-1-3?p=1081537#post1081537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- - Anything to do with modifying animals should require Science (Zoology or Vetinarian)</div> </div> </div> </div>So making a dog impossibly gain mass should use science? I somehow doubt that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1078007-rotes-of-life-1-3?p=1081537#post1081537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- - Any healing should require some medical skill - or something appropriate to the healing paradigm such as Esoterica (Reiki Healing)</div> </div> </div> </div>So your religious mage who simply heals with the power of god should know medicine? This seems against the theme of that sort of character.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1078007-rotes-of-life-1-3?p=1081537#post1081537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Creating an effect is not just about having the right spheres, the mage also needs the knowledge to encompass the effect they are creating!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So while I agree that there is more to Magick than spheres, I wouldn't peg it down to just knowledge or numeric ability ratings for that matter. I wouldn't be so quick to judge what you'd need for a certain effect and look at things on a case to case basis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T16:41:04-07:00","id":1081622,"title":"","content":"The only time you really need the skill to create something with magic is if the skill itself, or the process there in, is your focus for the effect.<br /> <br /> Of course you do need rudimentary knowledege of how things work and if you were to make a complex device that anyone can use you would then need the appropriate skills. <br /> <br /> Making giant bugs that spit poison and regenerate the swarm as they die off is si-fi enough that your imagination should suffice. Its not like you are introducing a new species that will continue on after you are done with them. Then all the knowledge skills would certainly be required.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T16:43:57-07:00","id":1081626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1078007-rotes-of-life-1-3?p=1081567#post1081567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't want your mage players to do weird stuff?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a difference between weird and silly","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T04:08:41-07:00","id":1081772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - Any 'clever' ideas should require a degree of skill (equal to sphere rating) in a suitable subject for the paradigm<br /> e.g.<br /> - - Anything to do with poisons should require the Poison skill (or Chemistry at a penalty)<br /> - - Anything to do with modifying plants should require Science (Botany)<br /> - - Anything to do with modifying animals should require Science (Zoology or Vetinarian)<br /> - - Any healing should require some medical skill - or something appropriate to the healing paradigm such as Esoterica (Reiki Healing </div> </div> </div>Why?<br /> Why should a Chorister asking The One for a miracle require any of that at all? Why would a Verbena require classic sciences?<br /> <br /> With the Exception of some mystical paradigms indeed requiring appropriate Esoterica for things like healing, as you mentioned, all those other things are mostly subject for technomagickal and technocratic paradigms.<br /> <br /> No Verbena would require Progenitor sciences for their healing and transmutations.<br /> Herbalism? Sure, that would fit quite well. But that again would depend on if the Verbena individual in question actually uses classic Herbalism for their poisons,or does it through curses and praying to the Old Gods.<br /> No Chorister would read up on Zoology before asking the The One for a deed. No Hermetic would consult Veterinarian sciences before drawing their sigils.<br /> <br /> The lack of need for those sciences is *exactly* the major difference between Magick and Science(!) in the first place, be it from a Technomagickal or Technocratic viewpoint. It's what the Technocracy is so up in arms about. That no proper, rational sciences are involved.<br /> <br /> <br /> One thing I fully agree on though is, that enforcing a sane and coherent paradigm in a player's Mage RP is the one thing to be used to prevent: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1078007-rotes-of-life-1-3?p=1081537#post1081537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How to stop your players getting away with wacky shit 101:</div> </div> </div> </div>That.<br /> <br /> <br /> A properly RPed paradigm is what prevents a Chorister or Verbena from putting out flying, poisonous hybrid monstrosities - at first. Most would regard it as a travesty on creation and nature. I don't even see how a Dreamspeaker or Akashic could do it in the first place with their usual paradigms, and a Cultist of Ecstasy would probably have to take in enough LSD to come up with those images and make them real, that it would leave the Cultist useless for anything else in that scene.<br /> <br /> Now, on the flipside, the insane Etherite might be ready to pump out the stuff - heck, it's their cliche spiel - but *they*, as you said, would need to be careful and 'scientific' - in the way that the Etherites do their whacko sciences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 04-21-2017, 07:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T06:59:07-07:00","id":1081815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1078007-rotes-of-life-1-3?p=1081626#post1081626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is a difference between weird and silly</div> </div> </div> </div>That's kinda relative. I consider a lot of classical magickal practice hopelessly silly.<br /> <br /> Like the supposed &quot;mounting&quot; of a hallucinogen laden &quot;flying broomstick&quot; or Nostradamus' love potion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":". 04-21-2017, 01:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T01:50:59-07:00","id":1082949,"title":"","content":"I agree that mythic mages do not need science to do their magic. However, they still should have skills and knowledges according to their paradigms. :like do, meditation and ezoterica for and akashiana. Occult and enochian for Hermetic and spirit knowledge for the shaman. <br /> Also, using those knowledge should provide bonus/lower difficulty of the magic. There is a section on that in either M20 or &quot;How do you do that?&quot; books Otherwise you may demand additional Spirit 2, that would reflect incantations to the appropriate spirits that govern the given magic or use of ephemera to correctly influence the material world. e.i. You want a pistol shrimp claws but haven't ever seen one and know no biology? Then prey to Poseidon, call shrimp spirit, download from the Net or dip into Akashic Records. <br /> Plus, don't forget to make the same call for the Technomancers. A progenitor NEEDS Science (Biology) and proper lab for his effects. He/she can't just grow claws, call to Odin and let it rip.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T03:42:00-07:00","id":1091884,"title":"","content":"Note that in my post above I was implying that Science(Botany) is not necessarily what we think of as modern science - it could just as easily represent the in depth knowledge that a druid would have, or a shaman of a jungle tribe. The name of the skill isn't important what matters is that the character have some knowledge of how things work that fits their paradigm and that when the player tries to do 'silly' stuff the ST has an excuse to make it difficult for them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}